Current situation:

Then started trying necromancers, which I have always liked.
After an army of them had entered the dungeon, finally one of
them stands on the vibrating square.

Unfortunately, on a save file, since I got tired on "casting spells
with your hitpoints". He has converted to lawful, however, and
is accompanied by several angelic beings... :)

Then I realized that flame and ice mages could twoweapon, so
there's also Job the flame mage, who had the opportunity to
wish for the Eye of the Aethiopica.

Job had to use several "swindling" techiniques: the jumping spell
to escape from a vampire lord at the bottom of the mines,
and the E-word several times. It also helped to find a wand of polymorph
on the first level, and the three initial spellbooks gave him a total
of 15 spells before the wand was drained. Create monster, healing and
magic missile being the worthwhile ones. A magic lamp was found
in the mines, and after 80 hp was gained, finally the Eye was wished
for. That was a lifesaver, since soon thereafter both the need for heavy
firepower (mm) and healing greatly increased. Obtained the Hand of
Vecna, but stupidly sacrificed it... oh well, after the frustration, decided
to keep going anyways.

And finally, some comments:

What can I say, I like the game! I like playing spellcasters, and I think
that finding a suitable ascension kit is greatly more challenging
than in plain NH. Now that dragon SM increases spell failure
even for wizards, the goal of obtaining ww/fly/mb+speed+
reflection+drain res (to wield Thiefbane) is by no means easy,
but fun!

Personally, I find it frustrating that the wizard's quest artifact has
such a powerful role when playing spellcasters. Sure, there's the
robe of power and the techniques, but still.

Has anyone ever used the spells enchant armor and weapon?
You'll need pretty good casting skills and level and by that time
you'll usually have enough scrolls anyways.

The spell of passwall is great, and IMHO well balanced, too.

(Mis)use of the flame sphere spell has resulted in several
premature deaths, but if skillfully cast, can be used to convert
the minetown into a cemetary... :)

In slash'em, wishing for quest artifacts is terribly hard, since by
the time you'll get a wish AND have the 80 hp required not to
die as a result, you've probably found enough artifacts on the
floor to make the wish impossible. Maybe that's as inteded to be.

Gypsies are an easy way to convert your gems into wishes.
Never tried reverse-genociding them, maybe that could be
an abuse? And if you run out of gems, just send in some diamond
or ruby golems.


